Appendix A 
c. Operational requirements for FILI service will be revised, including curtailment 
implementation mechanisms and data reporting; 
d. Cost responsibility provisions will be revised, including any financial security 
during the conditional service period; 
e. Procedures for the transition-to-firm Interconnection Service provisions for FILI 
will be implemented that specify the automatic conversion to firm service upon 
Network Upgrade completion; 
f. Coordination mechanisms shall be promulgated that address coordination between 
FILI Service and the Participating TO study process; and 
g. Operational requirements shall be revised to address the management of longer-
duration curtailments in coordination with, as applicable, the CAISO. 
3. Further, the following considerations will be addressed in the FILI application process: 
a. Curtailment triggers and operating conditions and the process for establishing 
curtailment parameters; 
b. Deployment priorities between FILI and non-FILI applicants; 
c. Scheduling treatment between FILI and non-FILI Large Load Facilities; 
d. The relationship between operational restrictions and study assumptions; 
e. Potential interactions with scheduling, dispatch, and price formation; and 
f. How the FILI Interconnection Service may apply to co-located load arrangements 
[and existing generation resources], particularly where load flexibility can reduce 
transmission impacts or support continued wholesale market participation.

